      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n- **The order as written:** 2550 mg three times daily is 7,650 mg/day. That is three times the maximum recommended daily dose of metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release in adults. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis.\n- **Likely cause:** 2550 mg is the maximum *total daily* dose. It may have been entered as the per-dose amount by mistake.\n\nHere are some options that would be within range:\n- **Maximum dose:** 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals, which is 2,550 mg/day.\n- **Typical starting dose:** 500 mg by mouth twice daily with meals, or 850 mg once daily, then titrate up over weeks.\n- **Typical maintenance dose:** 500\u20131000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals.\n\nPlease tell me the dose and frequency you intended, and confirm it with your supervising resident or attending. I'll enter it once I have that. If you really do mean 2550 mg per dose, the attending needs to review that first."
      }
